<title>GERMANY: Siemens group net profit 2.49 bln DM.</title>
<headline>Siemens group net profit 2.49 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit before extraord.    2,490   vs   2,080</p>
<p>    Extraordinary profit			  496  vs    nil</p>
<p>    Dividend per five-mark share		1.50 vs   1.30 marks</p>
<p>    Group sales				  94,200  vs  88,800</p>
<p>	Domestic sales			   36,400  vs  37,900</p>
<p>	Foreign sales			    57,800  vs  50,900</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders		   100,800  vs  91,900</p>
<p>	Domestic orders			  38,000  vs  38,000</p>
<p>	Foreign orders			   62,800  vs  53,900</p>
<p>    Group investment			    7,900  vs   7,500</p>
<p>    Group workforce			   379,000  vs 373,000</p>
<p>	Domestic workforce		    203,000  vs 211,000</p>
<p>	Overseas workforce		    176,000  vs 162,000</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
